Source: bulwark-desktop
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Viet Anh Nguyen <vietanh.dev@gmail.com>
# The desktop app's own source package, beside the CLI's `bulwark` source in the same PPA.
# Like the CLI, every crate is vendored into the source tarball and the build runs with
# CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true (Launchpad builders have no network); the frontend ships prebuilt in
# the tarball (see scripts/build-ppa-source.sh --package desktop for why). scripts/build-ppa-
# source.sh rewrites the cargo/rustc lines below to a versioned toolchain on series whose
# default is too old (noble: cargo-1.91), so keep each on a line of its own.
# The -dev packages are what the GTK/WebKit `-sys` crates link against through pkg-config;
# libdbus-1-dev is for libdbus-sys (notifications). libappindicator-sys dlopen()s its library
# at run time, so the tray needs it in Depends, not here.
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cargo,
 rustc,
 pkgconf,
 libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev,
 libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-dev,
 libsoup-3.0-dev,
 libgtk-3-dev,
 libayatana-appindicator3-dev,
 libdbus-1-dev,
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://bulwark.nrl.ai
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/vietanhdev/bulwark.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/vietanhdev/bulwark
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: bulwark
Architecture: any
# Named `bulwark`, like the package inside the GitHub release's bulwark-desktop_<v>_<arch>.deb,
# so this upgrades that install in place (<v>-0ppaN~<series>1 sorts above the release's plain
# <v>). It owns /usr/bin/bulwark-app and /usr/bin/bulwark, never /usr/bin/bulwarkctl, so it
# installs side by side with the bulwarkctl package.
# libayatana-appindicator3-1 is loaded with dlopen() for the tray icon, so dh_shlibdeps cannot
# see it (WebKit and GTK it derives from the binary's links).
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libayatana-appindicator3-1
# Same list as tauri.conf.json's deb "recommends"; keep them in step.
Recommends: clamav, openssh-client, curl, git, pkexec | policykit-1
Description: Linux security misconfiguration & intrusion scanner (desktop app)
 Bulwark scans a Linux host for security misconfigurations and intrusion
 indicators using a native Rust rule engine over declarative YAML rules, and
 explains findings in plain language with a suggested fix.
 .
 This package provides the desktop app (bulwark-app) and the command-line
 engine it uses for privileged scans (bulwark). It also installs a polkit
 policy that makes pkexec ask for the administrator password on every use.
 See the bulwarkctl package for the command line alone.
